IMPORTANT COMMANDS AND MEANINGS - mongod: starts a MongoDB server. -
mongosh: opens MongoDB Shell. - mongos: starts the query router. -
–configsvr: starts a config server. - –shardsvr: starts a shard
server. - –replSet: specifies the replica set name. - –dbpath: specifies
the data storage directory. - –port: specifies the port. -
rs.initiate(): initializes a replica set. - sh.addShard(): adds a shard
to the cluster. - sh.enableSharding(): enables sharding for a
database. - sh.shardCollection(): shards a collection using the
specified shard key. - sh.status(): displays cluster status. -
explain(“executionStats”): displays query execution statistics. - $gte:
greater than or equal to. - $lt: less than. - $match: filters
documents. - $group: groups documents. - $avg: calculates average.

